@startuml 11-per-host-block
!include theme-oriolrius.puml
title Per-host access block: one person, one server
left to right direction

rectangle "Host-CA revocations" as r1 <<danger>>
rectangle "User-CA revocations" as r2 <<danger>>
rectangle "Active blocks on db1\n(Alice's keys)" as r3 <<danger>>
rectangle "KRL(db1)\nsigned with the Host CA key" as krl <<file>>
rectangle "db1\nrefuses Alice" as db1 <<machine>>
rectangle "KRL(web1)\nno block" as krlw <<file>>
rectangle "web1\naccepts Alice" as web1 <<machine>>
r1 --> krl
r2 --> krl
r3 --> krl
r1 --> krlw
r2 --> krlw
krl --> db1 : next pull (~15 min)
krlw --> web1
note bottom of db1
  A block is NOT a revocation: Alice's certificate stays valid elsewhere.
  Blocks match keys: identities that share a key are blocked together.
  Needs krl-client. Optional SSH_BLOCK_ISSUANCE_GATE stops NEW certificates
  from opening the blocked host.
end note
@enduml
